That's great!  The core components of all OpenVPN products are open 
source, so you should find everything you need online.  For OpenVPN 
Access Server and OpenVPN Connect, there is no source code available for 
the proprietary bits.  But you are free to try to find security issues 
in any of our products.

If you find anything, please have a look at the "Report a security 
vulnerability" section here: https://openvpn.net/contact/

If you find critical issue, we kindly ask you to PGP encrypt the report 
you send to security@...2830...


